From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: notifications show the app icon, not a glyph at tile
 size

The Shelf island and the notification cards lead with the notifying app:
its full-colour icon, or a picture of the sender when the notification
carries one. Three things put a small symbolic glyph there instead.

The island decided glyph or artwork by asking whether any of the icon names
ended in -symbolic. Gio.ThemedIcon adds a -symbolic variant of every name
itself, so every app icon counted as a glyph and the island drew it at 16px
in its ink on a grey tile, for every app. It also read St.Icon:is-symbolic,
which the glyph style sets by loading the icon symbolic, so a glyph stayed
a glyph. isGlyphIcon() decides from the name asked for (or the file name),
and the card tile uses it too.

The daemon placed the sender by its process first and by the desktop-entry
hint only after that; a background agent, a portable app or a capsule runs
where the window tracker cannot place it, so the card fell back to the icon
the notification carried. The hint now comes first, and a name that is not
an exact desktop ID is matched loosely (case, a trailing ID component, the
window class, and for the app name the display name), counting only when a
single installed app answers.

A notification image replaced the card tile whenever it was not a themed
-symbolic icon, so a symbolic file became the tile. Only a picture does now:
image data, or a file that is not a symbolic asset. An app no one can name
with only a symbolic icon keeps the glyph tile, at glyph size.
---
 js/ui/lumaNotificationBeacon.js |  7 +++--
 js/ui/messageList.js            | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 js/ui/notificationDaemon.js     | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/js/ui/lumaNotificationBeacon.js b/js/ui/lumaNotificationBeacon.js
index e71ba76..b55255a 100644
--- a/js/ui/lumaNotificationBeacon.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaNotificationBeacon.js
@@ -441,10 +441,11 @@ class NotificationBeacon extends St.Button {
         // Until the island is first shown its icon has not loaded, so a
         // themed -symbolic name counts as a glyph as well (the first
         // notification otherwise showed its glyph bare, as artwork).
+        // The app's own icon is artwork whatever the island showed before it;
+        // see MessageList.isGlyphIcon for why neither is-symbolic nor every
+        // themed name can decide that.
         const gicon = this._markIcon.gicon;
-        const named = gicon instanceof Gio.ThemedIcon &&
-            gicon.get_names().some(name => name.endsWith('-symbolic'));
-        const glyph = this._markIcon.is_symbolic || named || !gicon;
+        const glyph = MessageList.isGlyphIcon(gicon);
         if (glyph && !this._markIcon.gicon)
             this._markIcon.icon_name = 'luma-bell-symbolic';
         this._mark.remove_style_class_name(glyph ? 'luma-notification-beacon-mark-art' : 'luma-notification-beacon-mark-glyph');
diff --git a/js/ui/messageList.js b/js/ui/messageList.js
index 8d8674e..40629e0 100644
--- a/js/ui/messageList.js
+++ b/js/ui/messageList.js
@@ -463,6 +463,34 @@ class MessageHeader extends St.BoxLayout {
     }
 });
 
+const SYMBOLIC_FILE = /-symbolic(\.[a-z]+)?$/;
+
+// Whether an icon is a glyph (drawn small, in the ink colour, on a tile)
+// rather than artwork shown whole. Decided from the icon asked for, never from
+// St.Icon:is-symbolic: the glyph tile's own style loads its icon symbolic, so
+// reading that back kept a tile a glyph once it had been one. Nor from every
+// name a Gio.ThemedIcon carries: it adds a -symbolic variant of each name
+// itself, so "any name ends in -symbolic" was true of every app icon, and the
+// Shelf showed every app as a 16px glyph.
+export function isGlyphIcon(gicon) {
+    if (!gicon)
+        return true;
+    if (gicon instanceof Gio.ThemedIcon)
+        return gicon.get_names()[0]?.endsWith('-symbolic') ?? true;
+    if (gicon instanceof Gio.FileIcon)
+        return SYMBOLIC_FILE.test(gicon.get_file().get_basename() ?? '');
+    return false;
+}
+
+// A notification image that is a picture of something (an avatar, a photo),
+// rather than an icon: a file or image data, and not a symbolic asset.
+function isPicture(gicon) {
+    if (gicon instanceof Gio.ThemedIcon)
+        return false;
+    // Image data (Gio.BytesIcon, a GdkPixbuf) is always a picture.
+    return !isGlyphIcon(gicon);
+}
+
